# After-plan review gate

> Install this rule **per consumer project** (`.cursor/rules/`), not as a user-global always-on rule.
> Reliable path: skill/command `finish-plan` (always sets the marker).

When you **finish executing an implementation plan** (all plan tasks done, or you are about to declare the plan complete):

1. Prefer invoking skill **`finish-plan`** (writes marker + asks HITL via `hitl-choice` (AskQuestion required; text only after failed/missing tool)).
2. If you cannot load that skill, still:
   - Create `.cursor/review-gate.pending` (one line `pending`)
   - **Stop** and ask via skill **`hitl-choice`** (AskQuestion required; preset Finish-plan HITL); text only after failed/missing tool:

   > Plan done. Want to do your own review first?
   > - `skip` — start engineer-reviewer now
   > - `approve` / `done` — start after your review
   > - or describe fixes first

3. Do **not** start `engineer-reviewer` / `/engineer-review` until the user replies `skip`, `approve`, or `done`. If they already replied one of those tokens after the gate was asked, do not re-ask — clear the marker and continue.
4. On that reply: delete `.cursor/review-gate.pending` first; on frontend ask for Figma URLs via `hitl-choice` Figma preset (or `no figma`); then run engineer-review. `skip` / `approve` / `done` all start review (they are not “skip review” / “close without review”).

Does not apply to pure Q&A, docs-only answers, or when the user already launched `/engineer-review` manually.
